Subject: [PATCH] unisocwifi: fix out-of-bounds write of per-TID ADDBA timestamps

struct sprdwl_peer_entry keeps the time of the last ADDBA attempt per TID
in "struct timespec time[6 + 1]", but prepare_addba() indexes it with the
frame's TID, which can be 7: the 802.11u QoS Map in change_priority_if()
assigns any UP 0..7, and 802.1Q tagged frames carry a 3-bit priority. A
TID of 7 writes a struct timespec past the end of the array.

Without further fields after time[] this overwrote the start of the next
peer_entry[] element (the next station's MAC address and LUT fields). With
the per-LUT counters of 150 directly after the array, it shows up on
hardware as rx_packets equal to the Unix time in seconds and rx_bytes
equal to a nanosecond value.

Size the array by IEEE80211_NUM_TIDS and refuse out-of-range TID and LUT
indexes, and a NULL peer, at the top of prepare_addba().

---
diff --git a/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c b/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c
index 2ded243..5ca8e11 100644
--- a/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/tx_msg.c
@@ -1210,6 +1210,10 @@ static void prepare_addba(struct sprdwl_intf *intf, unsigned char lut_index,
 		   struct sk_buff *skb, struct sprdwl_peer_entry *peer_entry,
 		   unsigned char tid)
 {
+	if (lut_index >= MAX_LUT_NUM || !peer_entry ||
+	    tid >= ARRAY_SIZE(peer_entry->time))
+		return;
+
 	if (intf->tx_num[lut_index] > 9 &&
 		peer_entry &&
 		(peer_entry->ip_acquired || !sprdwl_is_group(skb->data)) &&
diff --git a/unisocwifi/wl_core.h b/unisocwifi/wl_core.h
index ab3537b..5969291 100644
--- a/unisocwifi/wl_core.h
+++ b/unisocwifi/wl_core.h
@@ -77,7 +77,8 @@ struct sprdwl_peer_entry {
 	unsigned long ba_tx_done_map;
 	u8 vowifi_enabled;
 	u8 vowifi_pkt_cnt;
-	struct timespec time[6 + 1];
+	/* last ADDBA attempt per TID (prepare_addba() indexes this by TID) */
+	struct timespec time[IEEE80211_NUM_TIDS];
 
 	/* Host-side per-LUT traffic counters, reset when the LUT is added or
 	 * deleted. RX counts 802.3 MSDUs the firmware delivered for this LUT.
